            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of abdominal angina with percutaneous dilatation of an arteria mesenterica superior stenosis. Preliminary communication.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>43-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Percutaneous transluminal dilatation of an atherosclerotic stenosis of the superior mesenteric artery was done in a 65-year-old woman with abdominal angina. The patient was relieved of abdominal pain immediately after the dilatation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
